AudD  ·  profile default
                 │  Getting started   Guide   Commands  [Keys]  Exit codes and …
 1 Recognize     │ Everywhere
 2 Now playing   │   ctrl+k or :    command palette: run any command
 3 Streams       │   1-7            jump to a section
 4 History       │   ↑/↓ j/k        move in the sidebar
 5 Account       │   enter          open the section
 6 Settings      │   esc, ←         back (← from the left-most item)
*7 Help          >   ←/→            tabs and pages
                 │   click, wheel   select or press; scroll
                 │   y              copy the command shown at the bottom
                 │   ?              keys for this screen
                 │   F1             help
                 │   q              quit (ctrl+c always quits)
                 │ 
                 │ Mouse
                 │   Click a section, a page, a row, a field, or a button; click
                 │   a selected row again to open it. The wheel scrolls. To
                 │   select text with the mouse, hold Shift (Option in iTerm2).
                 │   AUDD_NO_MOUSE=1 turns the mouse off.
 ctrl+k commands │ 
 ? keys  q quit  │ Recognize
esc back  ↑/↓ scroll  ←/→ [ ] pages
ctrl+k runs any audd command